WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.203
- It's dessert time.

00:00:01.318 --> 00:00:03.901
(upbeat music)

00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:06.950
I'm James Briscione,
Director of Culinary Research

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:09.363
here at the Institute
of Culinary Education.

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:11.960
Today, we're taking your
candy aisle favorites

00:00:11.960 --> 00:00:13.240
and making a gourmet dessert.

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:14.073
Let's do this.

00:00:14.073 --> 00:00:16.285
First thing we're gonna
do is take some candy,

00:00:16.285 --> 00:00:19.010
cookies and ice cream and transform them

00:00:19.010 --> 00:00:20.320
into a beautiful tart.

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:23.320
We're gonna start here just
with a bit of vanilla ice cream.

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.723
Had that out to soften up a little bit.

00:00:25.760 --> 00:00:27.200
Might be a little runny,
but that's alright.

00:00:27.200 --> 00:00:28.033
Don't worry about it.

00:00:28.033 --> 00:00:30.280
And we're just gonna take
that, mix that that up.

00:00:30.280 --> 00:00:32.220
It's very soft, but we should be OK.

00:00:32.220 --> 00:00:33.053
We're gonna throw a little bit

00:00:33.053 --> 00:00:35.133
of candy and cookie into there.

00:00:35.270 --> 00:00:37.370
We're gonna take some of our cookies here,

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.960
chop them up, throw them right in.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:43.860
Some of the Reese's Pieces,
my personal favorite,

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.150
chop them up a little bit

00:00:45.150 --> 00:00:46.536
and they're going to get mixed in here

00:00:46.536 --> 00:00:48.250
with a bit of vanilla ice cream.

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:49.900
Get all that good stuff in there.

00:00:50.540 --> 00:00:52.610
If I were sitting at home,
no one else watching,

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:54.360
I'd be on the couch with this bowl.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:55.443
Done.

00:00:55.443 --> 00:00:56.910
But, we're gonna do this up.

00:00:56.910 --> 00:00:57.743
More cookies here.

00:00:57.743 --> 00:00:59.350
They're just gonna make
the base of our tart.

00:00:59.350 --> 00:01:01.050
None of these super fine,
they're kind of light,

00:01:01.050 --> 00:01:02.310
they have a little bit more texture,

00:01:02.310 --> 00:01:03.560
you get some of those creamy bits,

00:01:03.560 --> 00:01:05.340
you get some of the cookie bits.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.830
And we're just gonna take those

00:01:08.066 --> 00:01:12.113
and spread them in to the
base of our little molds here.

00:01:15.382 --> 00:01:17.143
So we're set with that.

00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:19.330
Then I'm just gonna
spoon that ice cream mix

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:22.210
right over the top to settle in

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:23.670
all those little nooks and crannies.

00:01:23.670 --> 00:01:27.370
And then just level the top,

00:01:27.370 --> 00:01:29.220
then here's where you can have some fun.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:31.070
We're gonna take these candies

00:01:31.490 --> 00:01:33.980
and just start lining
them up across the top,

00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:36.630
you can make any kind of
pattern or shape you want.

00:01:36.630 --> 00:01:38.640
May have gotten myself in
trouble with this idea.

00:01:38.640 --> 00:01:39.850
I was thinking monochromatic

00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.552
but it was gonna be way too
long to pick through all those.

00:01:41.552 --> 00:01:44.290
You can do this with any type
of candy, you could use M&amp;Ms,

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:45.840
now if you wanted to go Skittles

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.240
for a little more color you could,

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:49.780
but these ones with a nice
crisp shell like this,

00:01:49.780 --> 00:01:51.153
tend to do the best.

00:01:52.660 --> 00:01:54.113
OK, I made it.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.730
We're gonna take these off to the freezer.

00:01:55.730 --> 00:01:56.660
Let them set up.

00:01:56.660 --> 00:01:58.053
And we'll get back to it.

00:01:58.260 --> 00:02:00.170
Every great dessert needs a sauce.

00:02:00.170 --> 00:02:02.670
So we did here is we took a
little bit of heavy cream,

00:02:02.670 --> 00:02:05.590
some bourbon and strawberry fruit roll ups

00:02:05.610 --> 00:02:06.990
and just simmered those down

00:02:06.990 --> 00:02:08.650
so it was a nice thick creamy sauce.

00:02:08.650 --> 00:02:10.220
You kind of get a
strawberries and cream thing

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:11.330
with a little kick of bourbon.

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:12.163
I'm from the South,

00:02:12.163 --> 00:02:14.030
I love to throw a little
bit of bourbon in there.

00:02:14.030 --> 00:02:15.490
But look you don't have to have it at all.

00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:17.350
Just your fruit roll up
and a little bit of cream

00:02:17.350 --> 00:02:18.690
and you have a beautiful sauce.

00:02:18.690 --> 00:02:21.013
So we're gonna take a bit of that sauce,

00:02:21.099 --> 00:02:23.123
drop it right here on the plate.

00:02:24.480 --> 00:02:27.150
Get all the extra off the spoon
and then give it a little.

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.130
Perfectly sloppy.

00:02:28.130 --> 00:02:31.000
So that sets the frame for our plate.

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:31.833
We're gonna come back

00:02:31.833 --> 00:02:33.420
to that ice cream tart out of the freezer.

00:02:33.420 --> 00:02:35.063
I'm just gonna run this around.

00:02:35.350 --> 00:02:38.960
Lift it up, set it down right there.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:41.370
Looks fantastic, you've
got all those Oreo cookies

00:02:41.370 --> 00:02:42.203
on the bottom.

00:02:42.203 --> 00:02:44.410
That's actually beautiful
exactly as it is.

00:02:44.410 --> 00:02:45.770
But we can do better.

00:02:45.770 --> 00:02:47.460
I'm gonna take some fresh strawberries

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:48.870
and just kind of arrange them

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.170
around the edge coming down one side.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:54.220
We've got our Twinkies.

00:02:54.220 --> 00:02:55.978
Tear it up into some little chunks,

00:02:55.978 --> 00:02:58.843
kind of tuck it in there
with the strawberries.

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:00.840
You've got a like a little
strawberry short cake

00:03:00.840 --> 00:03:01.793
thing happening.

00:03:02.010 --> 00:03:03.193
Get that in there.

00:03:03.193 --> 00:03:04.543
Looking good.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.113
Bring it home with our mint.

00:03:07.580 --> 00:03:10.913
Just a couple nice fresh
leaves right in there.

00:03:12.127 --> 00:03:13.553
And there is it.

00:03:13.710 --> 00:03:15.693
Gourmet dessert out of the candy aisle.

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.080
You guys may think it's junk food,

00:03:17.080 --> 00:03:18.800
but you can have a lot of fun with this.

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:20.093
Put your own spin on it.

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.420
Plate it up beautiful,
let's see what you got.

